# Not part of the web app — excluded so Vercel's framework detector sees a Node project.
#
# ml/ holds the Python image-vulnerability pipeline. Its 38 .py files outweighed the app's
# 44 .tsx in Vercel's detector, which then tried to build this as a Python project and
# failed with:
#
#   No python entrypoint found. Set "tool.vercel.entrypoint" in pyproject.toml or define
#   an entrypoint in one of: app.py, index.py, server.py, main.py, ...
#
# Nothing at runtime reads from ml/ — only src/lib/image-ml/parity.test.ts does, and tests
# do not run on Vercel. If that ever changes, exclude a narrower path than the whole tree.
ml/

# Solidity workspaces: the Foundry harness and the PoC scripts. Neither is served.
foundry/
poc/
